    "Electrons — from acid to base",
    "Oxygen atoms — from base to acid"
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "why": "An acid is a proton donor and a base a proton acceptor (Brønsted and Lowry, 1923) — nearly every sharp taste and slick feel is that handover happening on your tongue or skin."
